requirement_id: "REQ-impl-region-transport"
reason: "Clause-scoped independent invariant checking, concrete-oracle examples, a bounded two-row registration fuzz grammar and actual selected generated-main construction-to-operand examples support conditional source-region transport. Complete invariant evidence across all five clauses remains outstanding: these finite shapes and input populations do not establish every admitted entry state, edge/backedge/phi, alias or summary allocation, captured environment, correlated aggregate, call/effect boundary and certificate dependency together. The current relation refuses unsupported calls/effects and retains imported initialization, intervening live-heap equality, concurrency, native and harness premises. This is an uncovered evidence obligation, not a demonstrated implementation contradiction; construction-to-operand provenance alone grants no whole-use or runtime authority. For the scheduled finite-occurrence route, the clarified inductive-transfer clause requires complete finite source-occurrence evidence: independently checked typed transfers cover every required edge and actual phi predecessor, all admitted initial states are included, and each residual frontier is independently unreachable. At each static boundary, its invariant is the union of complete correlated occurrence-entry relations, not independent component projections; a strictly decreasing well-founded occurrence rank establishes finite progress separately from that invariant. The discovery bound supplies no execution premise. This source-occurrence evidence and its full source/native composition remain pending; satisfying them alone does not resolve the broader existing transport evidence gap."
